From: Daniel <2660793+imDaniel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:33:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Validate cache salts before transport and snapshot Attention
 requests

Base: 1126 Attention fixes vLLM 44f3ee2ea2acd7aa70b12053c7f11d4d3d37c90c.
This change is independent of the tool encoder follow-up in this series.

Enforce the declared caller salt type when Python creates a wire request.
Recheck this mutable field in each multiprocess ADD entrypoint before
changing client state or encoding. The in-process path rechecks during
core preprocessing. Preserve valid empty salts.

Snapshot the sampling object and its steering arguments at admission on
Attention-enabled engines. In-process callers can reuse params while a
request is queued. Canonicalizing the shared object had modified caller
state, and a later edit could decouple the worker scale from its KV key.
The stock path on a server without Attention keeps its usual behavior.

Quality: Accepted scale values, operation, wire layout and block hashes
retain their existing semantics for unchanged inputs.

Tests: CPU-only input processor and direct wire construction, mutable
in-process request ownership with and without prefix caching, SHA-256
pickle/CBOR and existing multimodal/LoRA hash contracts. A mocked
transport exercises sync, async and DP dispatch after a caller edit.

Upstream status: downstream Attention maintenance.
